tion markets price Gonzalez near 83-84% to win", "R-leaning district (PVI R+3) keeps Republican upside alive"], "rationale": "The fundamentals point to a modest Democratic edge: incumbency and a strong money advantage for Gonzalez offset the district's Republican lean, and the lone recent poll shows him up three. Markets and most raters agree on a Democratic favorite, though the Tossup ratings from Cook and Inside Elections argue against a wider margin.", "watch": "A strong Republican national environment, boosted by high-profile GOP surrogates campaigning in South Texas, could tighten this into a true tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Vicente Gonzalez (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Vicente Gonzalez seeks another term in a South Texas district that leans Republican by about three points, facing Republican Eric Flores, who won his primary decisively and has raised nearly $2.9 million. Gonzalez has out-raised Flores and holds a large cash-on-hand edge, though Flores has benefited from some outside spending while Gonzalez has drawn little.\n\nRatings lean Democratic overall: seven of nine raters place the race at Lean D or better, while Cook and Inside Elections call it a Tossup. The one recent independent poll shows Gonzalez ahead by three, and prediction markets price his win chances in the low eighties. The combination points to a Democratic favorite in a competitive race.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7969, "margin": 4.84}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7826, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7895, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8125, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7373, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7369, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7694, "margin": 4.5}]}